{"name":"Chocolate Cosmos","hex":"#58111a","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"chocolate","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A food made from ground roasted cocoa beans.","A drink made by dissolving this food in boiling milk or water."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Made of or containing chocolate.","Having a dark reddish-brown colour/color."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/chocolate"},{"term":"cosmos","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The universe regarded as a system with harmony and order.\n\n A harmonious, ordered whole.","A harmonious, ordered whole."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of various mostly Mexican herbs of the genus Cosmos having radiate heads of variously coloured flowers and pinnate leaves."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cosmos"}],"entries":[{"title":"Chocolate Cosmos","blocks":[{"text":"Chocolate Cosmos  is a Japanese shōjo manga series written and illustrated by Nana Haruta. The series was serialized in Ribon magazine from the September 2007 issue of the magazine until its final chapter in the November 2008 issue. The individual chapters were collected into four tankōbon volumes by publisher Shueisha; the first on December 14, 2007, and the final on November 14, 2008."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/1/15/ChocolateCosmos2JP.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chocolate_Cosmos"},{"title":"Cosmos atrosanguineus","blocks":[{"text":"Cosmos atrosanguineus, the chocolate cosmos, is a species of Cosmos, native to Mexico. It has often been claimed that it is extinct in the wild; however it is truly abundant in Mexico. The species was introduced into cultivation in 1885, when the British seed company Thompson & Morgan first listed it in their seed catalogue. Its dark red to brownish red flowers have a scent resembling chocolate, which is one reason for its popularity as a cultivated plant."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/55/Cosmos-atrosanguineus.jpg/330px-Cosmos-atrosanguineus.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cosmos_atrosanguineus"},{"title":"Chocolate","blocks":[{"text":"Chocolate is a food made from roasted and ground cocoa beans. It can be a liquid, solid, or paste. It is eaten on its own and used to flavor other foods."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/11/Three_Bars_%281%29.jpg/330px-Three_Bars_%281%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chocolate"},{"title":"Cosmos","blocks":[{"text":"The cosmos is an alternative name for the universe or its nature or order. Usage of the word cosmos implies viewing the universe as a complex and orderly system or entity."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/15/The_Nights_Long_Moments_%28152181573%29.jpeg/330px-The_Nights_Long_Moments_%28152181573%29.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cosmos"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cb/Kakaw_%28Mayan_word%29.png/330px-Kakaw_%28Mayan_word%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cb/Kakaw_%28Mayan_word%29.png/330px-Kakaw_%28Mayan_word%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The Maya glyph for cacao","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AKakaw_(Mayan_word).png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/37/Aztec._Man_Carrying_a_Cacao_Pod%2C_1440-1521.jpg/500px-Aztec._Man_Carrying_a_Cacao_Pod%2C_1440-1521.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org